### Assets Inventory API - example flows
### Works with the REST Client extension (VS Code / JetBrains) or the IntelliJ HTTP client.
### Start the stack first: docker compose up -d && pnpm db:migrate && pnpm dev
### Also start the audit worker in a second terminal: pnpm worker:audit

@base = http://localhost:3000
@image = ./example-image.png

### Every request except login needs the session cookie: run the sign-in flow first.
### It sets a cookie jar, so later requests reuse the session automatically.

### 0. Authentication ---------------------------------------------------------

### Sign in as the SUPERADMIN (create one with: pnpm auth:create-superadmin)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana.ribeiro@example.com",
  "password": "SuperSecretDev123!"
}

### Who am I? (role + hasPassword, no secrets)
GET {{base}}/api/auth/me
Accept: application/json

### Wrong password -> 401 (unknown email returns the same message)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana.ribeiro@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Sign out everywhere: bumps sessionVersion, so old cookies stop working
POST {{base}}/api/auth/logout
Accept: application/json

### Change your own password (>= 12 chars, keeps this device signed in)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "SuperSecretDev123!",
  "newPassword": "AnotherStrongDev123!"
}

### Signing in is required -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{base}}/api/assets
Accept: application/json

### RBAC: a USER may read but not write -> 403 FORBIDDEN
POST {{base}}/api/asset-types
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Docking Station",
  "code": "DCK"
}

### 1. Asset types -------------------------------------------------------------

### List existing types (the seed creates Laptop, Printer, Router, Monitor)
GET {{base}}/api/asset-types
Accept: application/json

### Create a type (ADMIN+)
# @name createType
POST {{base}}/api/asset-types
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Docking Station",
  "code": "DCK"
}

### Duplicate code -> 409 CONFLICT
POST {{base}}/api/asset-types
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another Dock",
  "code": "DCK"
}

### Invalid code -> 400 with field details
POST {{base}}/api/asset-types
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Code",
  "code": "TOOLONG"
}

### Rename a type (ADMIN+; code is locked once assets exist -> 409)
PATCH {{base}}/api/asset-types/REPLACE_WITH_TYPE_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Docking Stations"
}

### 2. Assets ------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create an asset (ADMIN+): assetId is generated (IT-DCK-0001)
# @name createAsset
POST {{base}}/api/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetType": "DCK",
  "description": "WD19TB Thunderbolt dock",
  "unit": 1,
  "serialNumber": "SN-DCK-0001"
}

### Bulk item: several assets may have no serial number (empty string -> null)
POST {{base}}/api/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetType": "DCK",
  "description": "Spare USB-C cables (box of 10)",
  "unit": 10,
  "serialNumber": ""
}

### Duplicate serial number -> 409 CONFLICT
POST {{base}}/api/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetType": "DCK",
  "description": "Clashing serial",
  "serialNumber": "SN-DCK-0001"
}

### Search + filter (case-insensitive), paginated
GET {{base}}/api/assets?page=1&pageSize=20&q=dock&type=DCK&status=AVAILABLE
Accept: application/json

### Fetch one asset by human assetId (what a QR scan resolves) - includes history
GET {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001
Accept: application/json

### Update fields (ADMIN+; an ASSIGNER may send only {"status": ...}, assetId is immutable and ASSIGNED cannot be set here)
PATCH {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "WD19TB Thunderbolt dock (replaced cable)"
}

### 3. Images ------------------------------------------------------------------

### Upload / replace the single image (ADMIN+) (jpeg, png or webp, max 5 MB, magic bytes checked)
POST {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001/image
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

--Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="dock.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./example-image.png
--Boundary--

### Read the presigned imageUrl from the response above and download the object
GET {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001
Accept: application/json

### Remove the image (ADMIN+; object deleted from MinIO, imageKey cleared)
DELETE {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001/image

### 4. QR code ------------------------------------------------------------------

### PNG (inline)
GET {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001/qr
Accept: image/png

### SVG
GET {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001/qr?format=svg
Accept: image/svg+xml

### Attachment with filename IT-DCK-0001.png
GET {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001/qr?download=1

### 5. Staff -------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create staff (SUPERADMIN only). role: USER | ASSIGNER | ADMIN, plus a >= 12 char password
# @name createStaff
POST {{base}}/api/staff
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Diogo Alves",
  "department": "IT",
  "email": "diogo.alves@example.com",
  "phone": "+351 912 000 111",
  "role": "ASSIGNER",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery"
}

### Duplicate email -> 409 CONFLICT
POST {{base}}/api/staff
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Someone Else",
  "department": "IT",
  "email": "diogo.alves@example.com"
}

### Search staff
GET {{base}}/api/staff?q=it&page=1&pageSize=20
Accept: application/json

### Staff detail with currently assigned assets
GET {{base}}/api/staff/REPLACE_WITH_STAFF_ID

### Update staff: change the role, or reset somebody's password (revokes their sessions)
PATCH {{base}}/api/staff/REPLACE_WITH_STAFF_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+351 999 000 111",
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "password": "brand-new-password"
}

### The SUPERADMIN account cannot be edited or deleted through the API -> 403
PATCH {{base}}/api/staff/REPLACE_WITH_SUPERADMIN_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "renamed"
}

### 6. Assignments -------------------------------------------------------------

### Hand an asset to staff (ASSIGNER+; assigners may only target USER/ASSIGNER, never themselves)
# @name createAssignment
POST {{base}}/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetId": "IT-DCK-0001",
  "staffId": "REPLACE_WITH_STAFF_ID",
  "note": "loan for workshop"
}

### Same asset again -> 409 (already has an active assignment)
POST {{base}}/api/assignments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetId": "IT-DCK-0001",
  "staffId": "REPLACE_WITH_STAFF_ID"
}

### Active assignments only
GET {{base}}/api/assignments?active=true&assetId=IT-DCK-0001
Accept: application/json

### Assets currently held by a staff member
GET {{base}}/api/assets?assignedTo=REPLACE_WITH_STAFF_ID

### Delete staff while holding assets -> 409 CONFLICT
DELETE {{base}}/api/staff/REPLACE_WITH_STAFF_ID

### Record the return: asset goes back to AVAILABLE
POST {{base}}/api/assignments/REPLACE_WITH_ASSIGNMENT_ID/return
Accept: application/json

### Returning twice -> 422 UNPROCESSABLE
POST {{base}}/api/assignments/REPLACE_WITH_ASSIGNMENT_ID/return

### 7. Soft delete --------------------------------------------------------------

### Retire an asset (ADMIN+; image kept, nothing hard-deleted) -> 409 while assigned
DELETE {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001
Accept: application/json

### Confirm the assignment history survived
GET {{base}}/api/assets/IT-DCK-0001
Accept: application/json

### 8. Audit trail -------------------------------------------------------------

### Every action above was queued and written by the worker (pnpm worker:audit).
### SUPERADMIN only: rows contain actor emails and client IPs.
GET {{base}}/api/audit-logs?pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

### Filter by action, entity type, actor search or time window
GET {{base}}/api/audit-logs?action=ASSIGNMENT_CREATED
Accept: application/json

###
GET {{base}}/api/audit-logs?entityType=STAFF
Accept: application/json

###
GET {{base}}/api/audit-logs?q=role
Accept: application/json

### from/to are ISO-8601 bounds on occurredAt
GET {{base}}/api/audit-logs?from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2030-01-01T00:00:00Z&pageSize=20
Accept: application/json

### Everything an account did
GET {{base}}/api/audit-logs?q=ana.ribeiro@example.com
Accept: application/json

### Failed sign-ins and refused actions
GET {{base}}/api/audit-logs?action=AUTHORIZATION_DENIED
Accept: application/json

### Reading it needs SUPERADMIN; a USER gets 403 (and the denial is itself audited)
### Run this signed in as a non-superadmin to see it.